  "result": "`Cart.remove('sku-1')` now removes the Widget line, and all 7 tests pass.\n\n**Root cause:** in `shop/models.py:32`, `Cart.remove` matched lines on the item's name (`l.item.name != sku`) instead of its SKU. Calling `remove('sku-1')` compared `'sku-1'` with `'Widget'` and `'Gadget'`, found no match, and left both lines in the cart. `Cart.add` matches on `item.sku`, so the two methods weren't consistent.\n\n**Fix:** changed the comparison to `l.item.sku != sku`.\n\n**Checks:**\n- `python3 -m shop.demo` now prints `1`, so only the Gadget is left. Before the fix it would have printed `2`.\n- I added a regression test, `test_remove_by_sku`. It's in `tests/test_pricing.py` because there's no separate test file for the cart model.\n- I ran the suite with `python3 -m unittest`, since there's no `python` command on this machine.",
